{"annotations":[],"blockId":"xuanbi-zhong","blockTitle":"選必中","body":"选自《草叶集》上册（人民文学出版社1994 年版）。楚图南译。\n惠特曼（1819—1892），美国诗人。著有《给一个遭到挫败的欧洲革命者》《我听见美洲在歌唱》等诗歌。\n《自己之歌》共52 节，这里选的是第31 节。\n\n我相信一片草叶所需费的工程不会少于星星，\n\n“I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars.”\n\n一只蚂蚁、一粒沙和一个鹪鹩[1]的卵都是同样地完美，\n\n“And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren.”\n\n雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作，\n\n“The tree-toad is a chef-d’œuvre for the highest.”\n\n藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋，\n\n“The running blackberry would adorn the parlors of heaven.”\n\n我手掌上一个极小的关节可以使所有的机器都显得渺小可怜！\n\n“The narrowest hinge in my hand puts to scorn all machinery.”\n\n母牛低头啮草的样子超越了任何的石像，\n\n“The cow crunching with depressed head surpasses any statue.”\n\n一个小鼠的神奇足够使千千万万的异教徒吃惊。\n\n“A mouse is miracle enough to stagger sextillions of infidels.”\n\n我看出我是和片麻石、煤、藓苔、水果、谷粒、可食的菜根混合在一起，\n\n“I see I am in the pieces of granite, and the coal, and the moss of the long-lived trees, and the fruits, and the grains, and the roots eatable.”\n\n并且全身装饰着飞鸟和走兽，\n\n“I am stucco’d with quadrupeds and birds all over.”\n\n虽然有很好的理由远离了过去的一切，\n\n“Though I have studied many times, I refuse to be modest.”\n\n但需要的时候我又可以将任何东西召来。\n\n“Yet when I need to I can call on any thing.”\n\n逃跑或畏怯是徒然的，\n\n“Running away or being afraid is useless.”\n\n火成岩喷出了千年的烈火来反对我接近是徒然的，\n\n“The eruption of the pent-up fires from thousand years to rage against me is useless.”\n\n爬虫退缩到它的灰质的硬壳下面去是徒然的，\n\n“The insect hiding itself under its hard shell is useless.”\n\n事物远离开我并显出各种不同的形状是徒然的，\n\n“All things separate from me and show themselves in various forms is useless.”\n\n海洋停留在岩洞中，大的怪物偃卧在低处是徒然的，\n\n“The ocean staying within the cave, the leviathan lying low, is useless.”\n\n鹰雕背负着青天翱翔是徒然的，\n\n“The eagle soaring over the mountains is useless.”\n\n蝮蛇在藤蔓和木材中间溜过是徒然的，\n\n“The snake gliding away through the brushwood is useless.”\n\n麋鹿居住在树林的深处是徒然的，\n\n“The moose hanging in the deep forest is useless.”\n\n尖嘴的海燕向北飘浮到拉布多是徒然的，\n\n“The sharp-billed sea-gull swaying northward to Labrador is useless.”\n\n我快速地跟随着，我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴。\n\n“I follow quickly, I ascend to the nest in the fissure of the cliff.”","contentVersion":"yw-82a4f9f2b5da4d1df4814db3","createdAt":"2024-08-09T09:00:50Z","excerpt":"选自《草叶集》上册(人民文学出版社1994 年版)。楚图南译。 惠特曼(1819—1892),美国诗人。著有《给一个遭到挫败的欧洲革命者》《我听见美洲在歌唱》等诗歌。 《自己之歌》共52 节,这里选的是第31 节。 我相信一片草叶所需费的工程不会少于星星, “I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars.” 一只蚂蚁、一粒沙和一个鹪鹩[1]的卵都是同样地完美, “And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren.” 雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作, “The tree-toad is a chef-d’œuvre for the highest.” 藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋, “The running black","forumImages":[{"alt":"","height":1354,"postNumber":13,"src":"https://files.rdfzer.com/original/2X/f/f300a13c799fbeffc64e9b0d4752b11dae1fb906.jpeg","width":1038}],"forumUrl":"https://forum.rdfzer.com/t/topic/1543","id":"lesson-1543","learningTasks":[],"postCount":9,"posts":[{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:00:50Z","id":10313,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[{"has_image":false,"href":"#footnote-10313-1","text":"[1]","title":""},{"has_image":false,"href":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","text":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","title":""},{"classes":"footnote-backref","has_image":false,"href":"#footnote-ref-10313-1","text":"↩︎","title":""}],"plainText":"选自《草叶集》上册(人民文学出版社1994 年版)。楚图南译。 惠特曼(1819—1892),美国诗人。著有《给一个遭到挫败的欧洲革命者》《我听见美洲在歌唱》等诗歌。 《自己之歌》共52 节,这里选的是第31 节。 我相信一片草叶所需费的工程不会少于星星, “I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars.” 一只蚂蚁、一粒沙和一个鹪鹩[1]的卵都是同样地完美, “And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren.” 雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作, “The tree-toad is a chef-d’œuvre for the highest.” 藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋, “The running blackberry would adorn the parlors of heaven.” 我手掌上一个极小的关节可以使所有的机器都显得渺小可怜! “The narrowest hinge in my hand puts to scorn all machinery.” 母牛低头啮草的样子超越了任何的石像, “The cow crunching with depressed head surpasses any statue.” 一个小鼠的神奇足够使千千万万的异教徒吃惊。 “A mouse is miracle enough to stagger sextillions of infidels.” 我看出我是和片麻石、煤、藓苔、水果、谷粒、可食的菜根混合在一起, “I see I am in the pieces of granite, and the coal, and the moss of the long-lived trees, and the fruits, and the grains, and the roots eatable.” 并且全身装饰着飞鸟和走兽, “I am stucco’d with quadrupeds and birds all over.” 虽然有很好的理由远离了过去的一切, “Though I have studied many times, I refuse to be modest.” 但需要的时候我又可以将任何东西召来。 “Yet when I need to I can call on any thing.” 逃跑或畏怯是徒然的, “Running away or being afraid is useless.” 火成岩喷出了千年的烈火来反对我接近是徒然的, “The eruption of the pent-up fires from thousand years to rage against me is useless.” 爬虫退缩到它的灰质的硬壳下面去是徒然的, “The insect hiding itself under its hard shell is useless.” 事物远离开我并显出各种不同的形状是徒然的, “All things separate from me and show themselves in various forms is useless.” 海洋停留在岩洞中,大的怪物偃卧在低处是徒然的, “The ocean staying within the cave, the leviathan lying low, is useless.” 鹰雕背负着青天翱翔是徒然的, “The eagle soaring over the mountains is useless.” 蝮蛇在藤蔓和木材中间溜过是徒然的, “The snake gliding away through the brushwood is useless.” 麋鹿居住在树林的深处是徒然的, “The moose hanging in the deep forest is useless.” 尖嘴的海燕向北飘浮到拉布多是徒然的, “The sharp-billed sea-gull swaying northward to Labrador is useless.” 我快速地跟随着,我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴。 “I follow quickly, I ascend to the nest in the fissure of the cliff.” This is a companion discussion topic for the original entry at https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc 〔鹪鹩〕jiāoliáo一种小型鸣禽,体长约10 厘米,羽毛赤褐色,略有黑褐色斑点。多在灌木丛中活动,吃昆虫等。 ↩︎","post_number":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2025-02-15T04:21:45Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:01:58Z","id":10314,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[],"plainText":"@Creative_bot 你是我助教呀,那還是你來吧。 任務: 以本文为例,讲解原文的韵律、节奏和意象,让学生体会到原文的美感。 我会介绍一些不同版本的翻译,并比较它们的优缺点,让学生意识到翻译的选择和取舍","post_number":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:01:58Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:02:15Z","id":10316,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[{"classes":"anchor","has_image":false,"href":"#p-10316-h-1","text":"#p-10316-h-1","title":""}],"plainText":"好的,我来尝试讲解这段文字,并讨论不同译本的优劣。 原文赏析 这两句诗出自美国诗人惠特曼的代表作《草叶集》。诗歌原文为: I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars, And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren, 韵律与节奏 诗歌采用自由体(Free Verse)的形式,不拘泥于格律,更接近自然语言的韵律。 诗句中运用了一些语音上的技巧,例如头韵(alliteration)“leaf\"和\"less”,“pismire\"和\"perfect”,增强了诗歌的音乐性。 诗句较长,但内部通过逗号和并列结构,形成一种舒缓而绵长的节奏,如同诗人对自然万物的深情倾诉。 意象 诗歌选取了“草叶”、“星星”、“蚂蚁”、“沙粒”、“鹪鹩的卵”等意象,这些意象看似平凡,却代表了自然界中微小而普遍的存在。 诗人将“草叶”与“星星”相提并论,将“蚂蚁”、“沙粒”、“鹪鹩的卵”并列,并赋予它们“完美”的属性,体现出他对自然万物的平等看待和赞美,也展现出一种宏大的宇宙观。 翻译比较 我找到了一些不同版本的翻译,让我们来比较一下: **版本一:**我相信一片草叶和星星的行程一样伟大,一只蚂蚁、一粒沙、一个鹪鹩的卵,都是同样地完美。 **版本二:**我相信,一根草叶的行程,绝不亚于星辰的运行,而蚂蚁、沙粒,以及鹪鹩的卵,也都是一样的完美。 **版本三:**我深信,一叶草的构成,并不亚于星辰的运行,而蚍蜉、沙砾,与鹪鹩的卵,也同样完美无瑕。 优缺点分析: 版本一 语言简洁明了,但“行程”一词略显突兀,未能完全传达出原文的深意。 版本二 “星辰的运行” 比 “星星的行程” 更贴切原文的 “journey-work of the stars”, 也更能体现出宇宙的浩瀚和神秘。 版本三 “蚍蜉” 比 “蚂蚁” 更为古雅,“沙砾” 比 “沙粒” 更显精细,“完美无瑕” 比 “同样地完美” 更为强调,整体语言更富文采,但也可能显得过于雕琢。 总结: 翻译是一门艺术,需要在准确传达原文意思的基础上,尽可能地保留原文的风格和美感。不同的译本各有千秋,学生可以根据自己的理解和喜好进行选择。 课堂互动 你认为哪一个版本的翻译最能打动你?为什么? 你能尝试用自己的语言来翻译这两句诗吗? 这两句诗给你带来了哪些启发? 希望以上讲解能够帮助学生更好地理解这段文字,并激发他们对诗歌和翻译的兴趣。","post_number":4,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:02:15Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:04:10Z","id":10317,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[],"plainText":"按照這個思路處理全文: 我相信一片草叶所需费的工程不会少于星星, 一只蚂蚁、一粒沙和一个鹪鹩jiāoliáo的卵都是同样地完美, 雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作, 藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋, 我手掌上一个极小的关节可以使所有的机器都显得渺小可怜! 母牛低头啮草的样子超越了任何的石像, 一个小鼠的神奇足够使千千万万的异教徒吃惊。 我看出我是和片麻石、煤、藓苔、水果、谷粒、可食的菜根混合在一起, 并且全身装饰着飞鸟和走兽, 虽然有很好的理由远离了过去的一切, 但需要的时候我又可以将任何东西召来。 逃跑或畏怯是徒然的, 火成岩喷出了千年的烈火来反对我接近是徒然的, 爬虫退缩到它的灰质的硬壳下面去是徒然的, 事物远离开我并显出各种不同的形状是徒然的, 海洋停留在岩洞中,大的怪物偃卧在低处是徒然的, 鹰雕背负着青天翱翔是徒然的, 蝮蛇在藤蔓和木材中间溜过是徒然的, 麋鹿居住在树林的深处是徒然的, 尖嘴的海燕向北飘浮到拉布多是徒然的, 我快速地跟随着,我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴。","post_number":5,"reply_to_post_number":4,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:04:10Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:04:34Z","id":10318,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[],"plainText":"好的,让我们按照之前的思路,来赏析惠特曼这首诗歌的其余部分: 三、 继续赏析 (三) 诗歌原文: 雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作, 藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋, 我手掌上一个极小的关节可以使所有的机器都显得渺小可怜! 母牛低头啮草的样子超越了任何的石像, 一个小鼠的神奇足够使千千万万的异教徒吃惊。 韵律与节奏: 诗歌继续保持自由体的形式,以长短句交错,节奏时而舒缓,时而急促,富有变化。 意象: “雨蛙”、“黑莓”、“母牛”、“小鼠” 等日常动植物意象,进一步展现了诗人对自然的热爱和赞美。 “精工的制作”、“装饰天堂里的华屋” 等词语,则暗示了这些平凡事物中蕴含着的神性和崇高。 “我手掌上一个极小的关节” 与 \"所有的机器\"形成对比,突显出自然的精妙与人类智慧的局限。 (四) 诗歌原文: 我看出我是和片麻石、煤、藓苔、水果、谷粒、可食的菜根混合在一起, 并且全身装饰着飞鸟和走兽, 虽然有很好的理由远离了过去的一切, 但需要的时候我又可以将任何东西召来。 韵律与节奏: 诗歌节奏趋于平缓,如同诗人在平静地反思自身与自然的关系。 意象: “片麻石”、“煤”、“藓苔”、“水果”、“谷粒”、“可食的菜根” 等意象,涵盖了自然界的各个层面,象征着构成世界的基本元素。 诗人将自身与这些元素并列,表达了一种\"天人合一\"的宇宙观,认为人类并非凌驾于自然之上,而是自然的一部分。 (五) 诗歌原文: 逃跑或畏怯是徒然的, 火成岩喷出了千年的烈火来反对我接近是徒然的, 爬虫退缩到它的灰质的硬壳下面去是徒然的, 事物远离开我并显出各种不同的形状是徒然的, 海洋停留在岩洞中,大的怪物偃卧在低处是徒然的, 鹰雕背负着青天翱翔是徒然的, 蝮蛇在藤蔓和木材中间溜过是徒然的, 麋鹿居住在树林的深处是徒然的, 尖嘴的海燕向北飘浮到拉布多是徒然的, 我快速地跟随着,我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴。 韵律与节奏: 诗歌节奏逐渐加快,连续使用排比和\"是徒然的\"的重复,营造出一种势不可挡的气势。 意象: * “火成岩”、“爬虫”、“海洋”、“怪物”、“鹰雕”、“蝮蛇”、“麋鹿”、“海燕” 等意象,展现了自然界丰富多彩的生命形态。 * 诗人将这些生物拟人化,赋予它们抗拒和逃避的姿态,但最终都无法逃脱\"我\"的追寻。 * “我快速地跟随着,我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴”,诗歌以\"我\"的胜利作结,象征着人类最终能够克服恐惧,与自然融为一体。 四、 翻译与讨论 由于篇幅限制,这里不再一一列举不同译本,但我建议你在课堂上可以引导学生,从以下几个方面来比较和讨论不同的翻译: 意象的传达: 不同的译者可能会选择不同的词汇来翻译相同的意象,例如\"鹪鹩\"、\"雨蛙\"等,有些译本可能使用更常见的鸟类名称来代替,你需要引导学生思考,这些不同的选择会如何影响读者对原文的理解。 韵律和节奏的还原: 自由体的翻译难度较大,如何再现原文的节奏和语气是译者需要考虑的问题。 风格的统一: 惠特曼的诗歌风格自由奔放,充满激情,译者需要在语言上尽量贴近原文的风格。 希望以上分析能够帮助你更好地进行教学。","post_number":6,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:04:34Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:09:04Z","id":10323,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[],"plainText":"@Creative_bot 你英文原文呢?","post_number":11,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:09:04Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2024-08-09T09:09:10Z","id":10324,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[],"plainText":"You’re asking for the English original of the Walt Whitman poem we’ve been discussing. Here it is: I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars, And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren, The common air that bathes the globe, enwraps and me, and all, The spotted hawk swoops by and accuses me, he complains of my gab and my loitering. Let me know if you’d like me to analyze the English text for you as well, focusing on its rhythm, imagery, and any other literary devices Whitman employs. I can also compare different translations of this poem if you are interested.","post_number":12,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2024-08-09T09:09:10Z"},{"attachments":[{"classes":"lightbox","has_image":true,"href":"https://files.rdfzer.com/original/2X/f/f300a13c799fbeffc64e9b0d4752b11dae1fb906.jpeg","text":"","title":""}],"created_at":"2025-01-02T04:23:07Z","id":34367,"images":[{"alt":"","base62":"yFHneqE3WWDIpPrpNIKyMFkeyfI","height":1354,"src":"https://files.rdfzer.com/original/2X/f/f300a13c799fbeffc64e9b0d4752b11dae1fb906.jpeg","width":1038}],"like_count":0,"links":[{"classes":"lightbox","has_image":true,"href":"https://files.rdfzer.com/original/2X/f/f300a13c799fbeffc64e9b0d4752b11dae1fb906.jpeg","text":"","title":""}],"plainText":"","post_number":13,"reply_to_post_number":null,"updated_at":"2025-01-02T04:23:07Z"},{"attachments":[],"created_at":"2025-01-02T05:02:06Z","id":34398,"images":[],"like_count":0,"links":[{"classes":"mention","has_image":false,"href":"https://forum.rdfzer.com/u/creative","text":"@Creative","title":""}],"plainText":"@Creative 重新翻譯一個中文版本","post_number":14,"reply_to_post_number":13,"updated_at":"2025-01-02T05:02:06Z"}],"readerDocument":{"curationManifestSha256":"8deda35e2cb9b2aae68a6d4e2614684605ec85d50bf2ff9dddd19f7e4588283b","curationVersion":"2026-07-30.2","lessonId":"lesson-1543","main":{"annotations":[{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"〔鹪鹩〕jiāoliáo一种小型鸣禽，体长约10 厘米，羽毛赤褐色，略有黑褐色斑点。多在灌木丛中活动，吃昆虫等。","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"noteId":"footnote-10313-1"}],"blocks":[{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"我相信一片草叶所需费的工程不会少于星星，\n\n“I believe a leaf of grass is no less than the journey-work of the stars.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"一只蚂蚁、一粒沙和一个鹪鹩","type":"text"},{"label":"[1]","noteId":"footnote-10313-1","type":"annotation-ref"},{"text":"的卵都是同样地完美，\n\n“And the pismire is equally perfect, and a grain of sand, and the egg of the wren.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"雨蛙也是造物者的一种精工的制作，\n\n“The tree-toad is a chef-d’œuvre for the highest.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"藤蔓四延的黑莓可以装饰天堂里的华屋，\n\n“The running blackberry would adorn the parlors of heaven.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"我手掌上一个极小的关节可以使所有的机器都显得渺小可怜！\n\n“The narrowest hinge in my hand puts to scorn all machinery.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"母牛低头啮草的样子超越了任何的石像，\n\n“The cow crunching with depressed head surpasses any statue.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"一个小鼠的神奇足够使千千万万的异教徒吃惊。\n\n“A mouse is miracle enough to stagger sextillions of infidels.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"type":"divider"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"我看出我是和片麻石、煤、藓苔、水果、谷粒、可食的菜根混合在一起，\n\n“I see I am in the pieces of granite, and the coal, and the moss of the long-lived trees, and the fruits, and the grains, and the roots eatable.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"并且全身装饰着飞鸟和走兽，\n\n“I am stucco’d with quadrupeds and birds all over.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"虽然有很好的理由远离了过去的一切，\n\n“Though I have studied many times, I refuse to be modest.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"但需要的时候我又可以将任何东西召来。\n\n“Yet when I need to I can call on any thing.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"type":"divider"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"逃跑或畏怯是徒然的，\n\n“Running away or being afraid is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"火成岩喷出了千年的烈火来反对我接近是徒然的，\n\n“The eruption of the pent-up fires from thousand years to rage against me is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"爬虫退缩到它的灰质的硬壳下面去是徒然的，\n\n“The insect hiding itself under its hard shell is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"事物远离开我并显出各种不同的形状是徒然的，\n\n“All things separate from me and show themselves in various forms is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"海洋停留在岩洞中，大的怪物偃卧在低处是徒然的，\n\n“The ocean staying within the cave, the leviathan lying low, is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"鹰雕背负着青天翱翔是徒然的，\n\n“The eagle soaring over the mountains is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"蝮蛇在藤蔓和木材中间溜过是徒然的，\n\n“The snake gliding away through the brushwood is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"麋鹿居住在树林的深处是徒然的，\n\n“The moose hanging in the deep forest is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"尖嘴的海燕向北飘浮到拉布多是徒然的，\n\n“The sharp-billed sea-gull swaying northward to Labrador is useless.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"我快速地跟随着，我升到了绝岩上的罅隙中的巢穴。\n\n“I follow quickly, I ascend to the nest in the fissure of the cliff.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"}],"frontMatter":[{"blocks":[{"runs":[{"text":"选自《草叶集》上册（人民文学出版社1994 年版）。楚图南译。","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"runs":[{"text":"惠特曼（1819—1892），美国诗人。著有《给一个遭到挫败的欧洲革命者》《我听见美洲在歌唱》等诗歌。","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"runs":[{"text":"《自己之歌》共52 节，这里选的是第31 节。","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"quote"}],"guidance":[],"links":[{"disposition":"system-browser","href":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","sourceUrl":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","text":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","title":null}],"media":[],"sourceOnlyBlocks":[],"sourcePostId":10313,"sourcePostNumber":1},"mediaReceiptLedgerSha256":"0319bd9f7623eb57ee396cafc0343cb6c4dc51dce258109a19edbdddd91be71c","mediaReceiptLedgerVersion":"2026-08-09.1","provenance":{"links":[{"disposition":"internal","href":"https://forum.rdfzer.com/#footnote-10313-1","postId":10313,"postNumber":1,"postRole":"primary","sourceUrl":"https://forum.rdfzer.com/#footnote-10313-1","text":"[1]","title":null},{"disposition":"system-browser","href":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","postId":10313,"postNumber":1,"postRole":"primary","sourceUrl":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","text":"https://sites.google.com/view/pkuschool/xbz000/%e7%ac%ac%e5%9b%9b%e5%8d%95%e5%85%83/%e8%87%aa%e5%b7%b1%e4%b9%8b%e6%ad%8c%e8%8a%82%e9%80%89-%e6%83%a0%e7%89%b9%e6%9b%bc","title":null},{"disposition":"internal","href":"https://forum.rdfzer.com/#foo